<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch July-Sep unadj. unemployment down vs 1995.</title>
<headline>Dutch July-Sep unadj. unemployment down vs 1995.</headline>
<dateline>VOORBURG, Netherlands 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch non-seasonally adjusted unemployment came to an average of 441,000 in July-September 1996 versus 453,000 in July-September 1995, the Central Bureau of Statistics (CBS) said.  </p>
<p>DUTCH REGISTERED UNEMPLOYMENT NON-SEASONALLY ADJUSTED</p>
<p>			   July-Sept 96   June-Aug 96    July-Sept 95</p>
<p> total number	   441,000	  433,000	  453,000</p>
<p> pct of labour force    6.7		6.6		6.9</p>
<p>DUTCH REGISTERED UNEMPLOYMENT SEASONALLY ADJUSTED</p>
<p>			   July-Sept 96   June-Aug 96    July-Sept 95</p>
<p> total number	   441,000	  438,000	  453,000</p>
<p> pct of labour force    6.7		6.6		6.9</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
